{
  "title": "Work Health and Safety Act 2020",
  "abstract": "The Work Health and Safety Act 2020 is Western Australia's primary work health and safety legislation, which replaced the Occupational Safety and Health Act 1984. The Act commenced on 31 March 2022 and brings WA into the nationally harmonized WHS framework adopted across most Australian jurisdictions.\n\nThe Act establishes a primary duty of care for persons conducting a business or undertaking (PCBUs) to ensure, so far as is reasonably practicable, the health and safety of workers and others affected by the work. Officers (directors and senior executives) must exercise due diligence to ensure compliance with these duties.\n\nKey provisions include worker representation through Health and Safety Representatives (HSRs), enforcement powers for WorkSafe WA including improvement and prohibition notices, and industrial manslaughter provisions for negligent conduct causing death. The Act covers all workplaces in WA except mines and petroleum operations.",
  "keywords": ["legislation", "primary", "legal"],
  "targetAudience": [],
